{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018XXBoUcaV6SML464WymdYi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full experiment plan. Let me identify all the planned experiments (plan_001 through plan_010) and their current status from the registry. Let me map them:\n\n1. plan_001 (LoRA K=4 curated) → carr_quick_probe_03 → DONE\n2. plan_002 (LoRA K=8 curated) → carr_quick_probe_k8_02 → DONE\n3. plan_003 (LoRA K=4 random) → carr_baseline_no_curation_01 → DONE\n\n\n4. plan_004 (Full-FT K=4 curated LR=2e-5) → carr_fullft_k4_probe_03 → DONE\n5. plan_005 (Full-FT K=4 curated LR=5e-6) → carr_fullft_lr2e5_probe_01 → DONE\n6. plan_006 (Full-FT K=4 random LR=2e-5) → carr_fullft_lr2e5_nocuration_01 → DONE\n7. plan_007 (Full-FT K=16 extreme pressure) → carr_fullft_lr2e5_k\n\n16_probe_01 → DONE\n8. plan_008 (C1 regen) → c1-regen-v2 → DONE\n9. plan_009 (Qwen2.5-1.5B curated) → carr_qwen25_1-5b_lora_k4_curated → QUEUED\n10. plan_010 (Qwen2.5-1.5B random) → carr_qwen25_1-5b_lora_k4_random → QUEUED\n\nSo plans 009 and 010 are still queued—those are the cross-model experiments with the smaller Qwen model. But looking back at what the user actually asked for, they want detailed imagined data generated for every planned experiment in the median tier, not just the completed ones.\n\nThe tricky part is that the 0.6B experiments already have real results, so the median tier scenario doesn't change those—they're actual data. The median tier really comes into play when interpreting what the 1.5B cross-model experiments (plans 009 and 010) would show. I need to think about what the user is really asking for: predictions of what each experiment's results would look like if the median scenario holds true. I'm looking at the metric ranges for the 1.5B experiments under the median tier scenario—things like Vendi score changes, format entropy drops, and nearest neighbor distances—to establish what the predicted data should